  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1220 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nLong-term forecast impacts: Warm-up through Thanksgiving weekend. \nDry weather expected.\n\nDiscussion: Our warm-up won't be immediate. Thanksgiving Day itself \nis likely to be much cooler than normal across our area as the \nTuesday/Wednesday troughs phase across the Southeast and keep us in \ncool northwest flow. Beyond that, though, the pattern in the United \nStates looks much more longwave-oriented with long periods of zonal \nflow across the Rockies from Friday - Sunday. This will bring \nsoutherly winds and warming temperatures. Given the complete \nscouring of moisture from the boundary layer across the southern \nPlains, we'll stay dry across those first several days of return \nflow. Ensemble guidance is hinting at a trough passage early next \nweek, but details remain to be seen regarding just how much moisture \nthat trough will have available.\n\nMeister",
